  <wpt lat="49.663810119228174" lon="-110.27251818621224">
    <name>Route Alternative</name>
    <cmt>control</cmt>
    <desc>Riders who wish not to take the trail option through the park can follow this route towards the Sask boarder. Take the main road (Bull Trail) south and then Reesor road east. This is a more weather-resistant option than the trails, which can be muddy in wet conditions. </desc>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>checkpoint</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="50.16451711311703" lon="-112.56119534762705">
    <name>Route Alternative</name>
    <cmt>control</cmt>
    <desc>Riders who prefer to ride pavement can stay on Hwy 526 here going east and then take Hwy 36 (Veterans Memorial Hwy) south to meet up with the route.</desc>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>checkpoint</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="49.67377108786212" lon="-110.1470725104089">
    <name>Route Alternative</name>
    <cmt>control</cmt>
    <desc>Riders can choose to stay on Reesor Lake Road instead of taking trail. A good option in wet conditions where the trails will be muddy. </desc>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>checkpoint</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="49.67396861474111" lon="-110.14745759829619">
    <name>Reesor Hills Trail</name>
    <cmt>trailhead</cmt>
    <desc>Expect some challenging bits on this trail.</desc>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>info</type>
  </wpt>
